[sub_resource type="RectangleShape2D" id="RectangleShape2D_kill"]
size = Vector2(8000, 40)

; A wide floor built almost entirely out of #18's crumbling ledge, all at the
; same height so no side of it is the "high ground" -- four 200x24 ledges
; strung out with 40-70 px gaps between them, wide enough to cross with an
; ordinary swing but wide enough to fall through if nobody is moving.
; Standing still is the mistake: whichever ledge a player parks on starts its
; warning the moment they land on it, and 0.8 s later it is gone for three
; seconds. With two players loose on the same floor, that clock is always
; running on somebody.
;
; Island is the one permanent piece, centred and deliberately small -- 140 px
; against each ledge's 200, room to stand and not much more. It is not a
; balance choice: it is what keeps this stage from being able to erode to
; nothing under both players at once and deadlock the round with no floor
; left anywhere. Both spawns sit on top of it rather than on a ledge, so a
; round never opens with a countdown already ticking on the ground a player
; was just placed on (US-7) -- the erosion starts only once a player leaves
; home and stands on the wide floor built to fall out from under them.
;
; Ledge timings are left at CrumblingLedge's defaults (0.8 s warning, 3 s
; away), same as Highrise's Ledge3: one swing's worth of warning to commit to
; the next foothold or fall back, and long enough away that a ledge someone
; just lost is not simply waiting to be walked straight back onto.

